WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.934
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.169
We are hanging out
with Dave Chappelle,

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.170
ladies and gentleman.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.272
Now -- [ Laughs ]
Yeah!

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:10.476
Now, Dave, you are one of
my favorite comedians,

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:11.611
one of the best out there,

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.079
and you have such
a unique perspective,

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.249
so I thought that you could
help settle some of the biggest

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.785
and most important debates
of all time.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.420
Are you ready for this?

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.954
-I'll do --
I'll do what I can.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.156
-Okay.
Let's do it.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.991
It's time for
"Dave Chappelle Settles It."

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:28.060
-♪ Dave Chappelle settles it ♪

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.364
♪ Dave Chappelle settles it ♪

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.299
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.501
-All right, here we go.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:39.739 line:0%
First up --
small town or big city?

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.674 line:0%
-Depends on what I'm doing.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.976 line:0%
-[ Laughs] Ah!
Okay.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:47.079 line:0%
-All right. Obviously,
I'm a small-town kind of guy.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:52.051 line:0%
-Yeah.
Mac 'n' cheese -- fork or spoon?

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.619 line:0%
-You know,
I would hate to guess --

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.688 line:0%
A white person
must have asked this question.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.592 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.828 line:0%
That's fork food, baby.
-Yeah, fork.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.362 line:0%
You gotta do the fork, yeah.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.598 line:0%
-Who has soupy mac 'n' cheese?

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.600 line:0%
♪ White people ♪

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.871 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.307 line:0%
-All right. Here's something
everyone's talking about.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:19.111 line:0%
Cryptocurrency or cash?

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:20.814 line:0%
-Cash rules
everything around me.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:24.183 line:0%
In fact, I don't think you can
buy cryptocurrency without cash.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:25.618 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
There you go.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.353 line:0%
Yeah, that's actually right.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.788 line:0%
Now we're going
to a music topic here.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:32.492 line:0%
Ready for this?
Jazz or hip-hop?

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.360 line:0%
-Well, that's just not fair.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.263 line:0%
-Oh! This is
the debates of all time.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.165 line:0%
You have to settle it --
jazz or hip-hop?

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.567 line:0%
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.034 line:0%
-Jazz.
Sorry, Tariq.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:49.842 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:54.380 line:0%
-A follow-up --
guitar solos or drum solos?

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.015 line:0%
I know you like --
-This is a tough one,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.283 line:0%
because Amir's
sitting over there,

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.152 line:0%
and I know John Mayer's
probably watching like,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:02.021 line:0%
"Well, what is it?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.957 line:0%
-I'm a Black dude.
Drums all day, baby.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.258 line:0%
-There you are.
Very good.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.629 line:0%
Next up,
"Call of Duty" or "Fortnite"?

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.431 line:0%
-Well, that's easy --
"Call of Duty."

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.731 line:0%
-There you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:14.934 line:0%
"Fortnite" is the crack
of video games.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.337 line:0%
I don't even touch that stuff.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:19.605 line:0%
-I haven't
messed with it, either.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.774
'Cause I know --
I know I'll get addicted to it.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.609
I can't even look at it.
-I'm sure.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.245
-I haven't even opened it up.
I just know --

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.313
-I got my son
a copy of "Fortnite,"

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.516
I didn't see him for six months.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.518
-All right,
let's go into fashion here.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.554 line:0%
Skinny jeans or baggy jeans?

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:37.357 line:0%
-I'm not even
wearing pants right now, Jimmy.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:41.394 line:0%
-Okay, very good.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.195 line:0%
-I think,
yeah, neither one for me.

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:45.031
Skinny, baggy?

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.234
You can't go too skinny.
I can't do too skinny jeans.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.303
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Groans ]

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:54.807
Because you'd never wear pants
so tight that you have to decide

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.776
which leg your penis goes in.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:03:02.515
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.682 line:0%
-Summer's coming up.

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:09.621 line:0%
We need to know,
are sandals shoes?

00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:12.124 line:0%
-Oh, now
this is a good question.

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:15.728 line:0%
I'm gonna do
a full-throated no on that.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:19.732 line:0%
If they were shoes, then the
word "sandals" would not exist.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.901 line:0%
-Wow.
That's -- wow.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.103 line:0%
That was just --
-They'd just call them shoes.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.839 line:0%
-Yeah, I totally agree.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.408 line:0%
Do you think Jesus wore sandals?

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:32.679
-Uh, when he wore footwear,
I would imagine he did.

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.813
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:37.417
You know,
I would imagine, in those times,

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.086
sandals were a luxury item.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.622
-Yeah, that's what I think, too.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.524
-Could you imagine
if I time-travelled

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.026
and went back to biblical times
with some Timberlands on?

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.195
I would blow
their [bleep] minds.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:52.265
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:55.167
-Oh, we have I big one here.
This one's -- All right.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:04:00.672 line:0%
Best chicken sandwich --
Chick-fil-A or Popeyes?

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:04.243 line:0%
-You know, I'm gonna --
I don't know that I've

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.245 line:0%
eaten either
of those chicken sandwiches,

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:09.182 line:0%
but that Popeyes one looks like
it really caught traction.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.217 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:14.052 line:0%
-It is -- It is kind of insane.
It's unbelievable.

00:04:14.052 --> 00:04:15.821 line:0%
I know you like music,
so I keep going back to music.

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:18.958 line:0%
Best way to enjoy a concert --
standing or sitting?

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.627 line:0%
I wrote this one.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.494 line:0%
-Okay.
This is a very good question.

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:24.130 line:0%
-Thank you.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:28.634 line:0%
-I'm gonna have to say,
if I'm at a music show,

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.170 line:0%
I'd rather be standing.
-Correct.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.172 line:0%
-If I'm at a strip club,
I'd rather be sitting.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:38.911 line:0%
-All right, all right, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.880 line:0%
All right.
Dave, how about this one?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.083 line:0%
Should you know
your neighbors' names?

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:48.021 line:0%
-I should, but I don't.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:52.591 line:0%
-Here's another one.
Kayak or canoe?

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:55.995 line:0%
-Uh, I'm a canoe guy.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:59.899 line:0%
-I'm a canoe guy, too, but
I feel like I could be swayed.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.034 line:0%
-To the kayak world?
-Yeah, I could be in --

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.536 line:0%
-Kayak people look weird.
They just look lonely.

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:07.039 line:0%
The one stick, and the...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.475 line:0%
It just looks like --
You know what I mean?

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:14.213 line:0%
-All right, which is better --
finished basement or nice yard?

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:17.583 line:0%
-Ooh, boy. Now this is
a poor-person question.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:20.219 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.922 line:0%
Kind of person with my kind of
money is gonna be,

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.625 line:0%
"Should I finish the basement
or mow the grass?"

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:29.228 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.663 line:0%
-Yeah, all right.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.298 line:0%
-Finished basement.
Final answer.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.766 line:0%
-There you go.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:39.105 line:0%
When it comes to cooking,
half-baked or infused?

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:42.875 line:0%
Ah!
A little inside fun for you.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.744 line:0%
-All right.
Uh, uh...

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.979 line:0%
You know what, man?
I went through one of those

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.248 line:0%
weed-infused dinners once.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.083 line:0%
We was talking about
mac 'n' cheese.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:54.353 line:0%
I ate this mac 'n' cheese.
I didn't know it had weed in it.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:57.156 line:0%
And then I saw my mother, and
she goes, "Son, you look tired,"

00:05:57.156 --> 00:06:00.193 line:0%
and I said "Mama,
I'm high on mac 'n' cheese."

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.495 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:03.896 line:0%
She knew something was wrong,

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.797 line:0%
because I was eating it
with a spoon.

00:06:05.797 --> 00:06:07.033 line:0%
Nailed it.
-Aw! Come on!

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.501 line:0%
That's how you do it!
Come on, now.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.369 line:0%
Dave Chappelle,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.238 line:0%
That's how
you do it right there!

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:13.839
That's what I'm talking about!

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.608
Check out his podcast,
"The Midnight Miracle,"

00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:18.544
